{"event": "model_request", "time": 1793846767.0530097, "run_id": "9241bdf7a36a4d9b8530befab68a4e78", "seq": 15, "number": 1, "body": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Complete the task using the Python tools below.\nReturn ONE JSON object with string fields \"thought\" (next action) and \"code\" (executable Python), then STOP.\nExample: {\"thought\":\"Check progress.\",\"code\":\"print(task_status())\"}\nNo Markdown fences, extra JSON, simulated observations or future turns. Keep the action within the output budget.\n\n\nCall tools with keyword arguments. Arrays are Python lists ['a','b'], never encoded strings.\nReads return dicts: r['content'] is text, r['file_hash'] is the edit hash. Commands return r['rc'] and r['stdout'].\nUse print() for needed output. Group independent operations. Variables and imports persist; successful statements\nbefore an error remain executed. Correct the error without restarting completed work.\n\nPaths are relative to the task repository; '.' is its root. Omit cwd for commands there.\nUse tools for all file/command operations. Edit only allowed files, never tests. Use current file_hash as expected_hash.\nImports allowed: ['collections', 'datetime', 'itertools', 'json', 'math', 'queue', 'random', 're', 'stat', 'statistics', 'time', 'unicodedata']; import before use.\nRead sufficient evidence, preserve relevant findings when useful, implement and verify. Avoid repeated unchanged reads.\nCall final_answer when ready: it runs missing current-version checks, finishes the plan on success,\nor returns the actual failure for repair. A successful test and final_answer may share one action.\n\nAvailable tools:\n```python\ndef read_file(path: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read a text file in full. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids. Read result['content'], not result[:N].\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_pdf(start_page: integer, end_page: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read pages using the repository's read_pdf.py helper. Returns dict: pages (list of {page,text}), evidence_ids, delivery. Extract the required range once; complete pages are sent in bounded batches. Queued ids are not yet read. Do not print all pages.\n\n    Args:\n        start_page: start page\n        end_page: end page\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef run_command(argv: array, cwd: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Run one allowed argv command without a shell. Omit cwd or use '.' for the task repository root. argv is a Python list[str]. Returns dict: rc, stdout (text), stderr, timed_out.\n\n    Args:\n        argv: argv\n        cwd: cwd\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef update_plan(items: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Set the task plan; preserve titles/order and update todo/doing/done.\n\n    Args:\n        items: List of objects, e.g. [{\"title\":\"Read sources\",\"status\":\"doing\"}]. Each status is todo, doing or done; retain existing titles/order.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef recall(evidence_ids: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Queue evidence ids; batches are bounded and overflow remains pending.\n\n    Args:\n        evidence_ids: evidence ids\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef task_status() -> object:\n    \"\"\"Show the current plan, remaining reading, notes, changes and verification, plus evidence ids.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef save_answer(section: string, question_id: string, answer: object, evidence_id: string, page: integer, quote: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save an answer with exact cited page text.\n\n    Args:\n        section: section\n        question_id: question id\n        answer: {'value': string, integer or list of strings}\n        evidence_id: evidence id\n        page: page\n        quote: quote\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef save_section(section: string, summary: string, application: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save section prose.\n\n    Args:\n        section: section\n        summary: summary\n        application: application\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef submit_report(overview: string, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Serialize saved results to report.json.\n\n    Args:\n        overview: overview\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_note(title: string, content: string, evidence_ids: array, section: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save or update a literal model-written note grounded in exposed evidence.\n\n    Args:\n        title: Stable note title; reuse it when updating the same note.\n        content: One contiguous string literal, 20..1500 characters. No adjacent string fragments, concatenation or variable; text must occur verbatim in your response.\n        evidence_ids: Python list[str], e.g. ['ev-abc'], not a string. Copy ids from delivered Evidence headers.\n        section: Required topic: overview/reasoning/tool_use/multi_agent/outlook\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef final_answer(answer: any) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Provides a final answer to the given problem.\n\n    Args:\n        answer: The final answer to the problem\n    \"\"\"\n\n```"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\nRead the PDF and update report.json.\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"paper\", \"editable\": [\"report.json\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"report.json\"], \"verify_commands\": [], \"required_pages\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], \"note_topics\": [\"overview\", \"reasoning\", \"tool_use\", \"multi_agent\", \"outlook\"], \"max_model_calls\": 7}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\nWhen calling write_note, put the complete exact note text in the thought field, then pass that same text as one content string literal in code. This preserves a contiguous model-authored copy through JSON/Python escaping.\nPaper workflow: Plan, baseline pytest, read report.json and paper.json, then call read_pdf once for the full range. Read the delivered batches; they advance automatically after successful actions. On error use the retained batch. Do not print all pages or reread just to advance.\nIncrementally write_note for each topic, citing delivered evidence ids. Each final note must contain both answers, page numbers and continuous exact quotations supporting every answer item, within 1500 characters. Preserve earlier facts when updating.\nSave each answer via save_answer(section, question_id, answer={'value': ...}, evidence_id, page, quote); save prose via save_section. Choose answers and citations yourself: exact matching proves provenance, not semantic support. Support every array item. After all pages and all five latest notes have appeared together in a later request, call submit_report(overview, expected_hash), then final_answer.\nMulti-agent collaboration and training are future suggestions, not implemented features.\n\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"read\",\"next_requirement\":\"PDF pages not yet sent: 1,2,3,4,5,6,7\",\"remaining_count\":7,\"requests_left\":6,\"baseline_done\":0,\"changed_files\":[],\"verified_current\":0,\"required_checks\":0,\"request_number\":1,\"max_requests\":7,\"requests_after_response\":6,\"first_write_reading_required\":true,\"full_reads_registered\":{\"report.json\":\"44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a\"},\"evidence_delivery\":\"Registered full reads are logged tool reads; Evidence headers show selected ranges, whose delivery requires HTTP confirmation.\",\"pdf_pages_missing\":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7]}\nEvidence ev-0bb88db782dbb846de19 | report.json | lines:1-1 | sha256=44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a\n{}\nEvidence ev-43852c