summary\n        application: application\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef submit_report(overview: string, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Serialize saved results to report.json.\n\n    Args:\n        overview: overview\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_note(title: string, content: string, evidence_ids: array, section: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save or update a literal model-written note grounded in exposed evidence.\n\n    Args:\n        title: Stable note title; reuse it when updating the same note.\n        content: One contiguous string literal, 20..1500 characters. No adjacent string fragments, concatenation or variable; text must occur verbatim in your response.\n        evidence_ids: Python list[str], e.g. ['ev-abc'], not a string. Copy ids from delivered Evidence headers.\n        section: Required topic: overview/reasoning/tool_use/multi_agent/outlook\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef final_answer(answer: any) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Provides a final answer to the given problem.\n\n    Args:\n        answer: The final answer to the problem\n    \"\"\"\n\n```"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\nRead the PDF and update report.json.\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"paper\", \"editable\": [\"report.json\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"report.json\"], \"verify_commands\": [], \"required_pages\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], \"note_topics\": [\"overview\", \"reasoning\", \"tool_use\", \"multi_agent\", \"outlook\"], \"max_model_calls\": 7}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\nWhen calling write_note, put the complete exact note text in the thought field, then pass that same text as one content string literal in code. This preserves a contiguous model-authored copy through JSON/Python escaping.\nPaper workflow: Plan, baseline pytest, read report.json and paper.json, then call read_pdf once for the full range. Read the delivered batches; they advance automatically after successful actions. On error use the retained batch. Do not print all pages or reread just to advance.\nIncrementally write_note for each topic, citing delivered evidence ids. Each final note must contain both answers, page numbers and continuous exact quotations supporting every answer item, within 1500 characters. Preserve earlier facts when updating.\nSave each answer via save_answer(section, question_id, answer={'value': ...}, evidence_id, page, quote); save prose via save_section. Choose answers and citations yourself: exact matching proves provenance, not semantic support. Support every array item. After all pages and all five latest notes have appeared together in a later request, call submit_report(overview, expected_hash), then final_answer.\nMulti-agent collaboration and training are future suggestions, not implemented features.\n"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Course progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"read\",\"next_requirement\":\"write/reuse final section note: overview\",\"remaining_count\":6,\"requests_left\":2,\"baseline_done\":0,\"changed_files\":[],\"verified_current\":0,\"required_checks\":0,\"request_number\":5,\"max_requests\":7,\"requests_after_response\":2,\"first_write_reading_required\":true,\"full_reads_registered\":{\"report.json\":\"44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a\"},\"evidence_delivery\":\"Registered full reads are logg